Just for your info. Considering application of Ci/uV -> Cii/uuV to fu'ivla,=
=20
not only those beginning with CgV but also those in the form (C)V(g)CCgV...=
=20
produce tosmabru-like problem. I picked up such fu'ivla from an xml dump=20
dated 2015-01-08:

eskua, februa, fiakre, fiesta, kuadranta, kuaidzi, madjio, matriocka,=20
patriarko, reskuamata, restuatara, tiatro, tuitsku

For example, {februa} will be {fe + bruua} by adding u. In this case, the=
=20
apostrophe-method is also inapplicable because {febru'a} is in lujvo form.

If we require that ii or uu should be fully within the same word, this=20
problem will not occur, though.



